        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(microsoft-foundry): bound az subprocess lifetime on exec timeout",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`execFileSync` default `killSignal` is `SIGTERM`. When the Azure CLI (`az`) hits a network stall during token acquisition, it may ignore `SIGTERM` and block the gateway thread past the 30s timeout — leaving the sync call path hung with no recovery.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdding `killSignal: \"SIGKILL\"` to the `execFileSync` call ensures the `az` subprocess is forcefully terminated when the 30s timeout fires.\n\nThe async counterpart `execAzAsync` calls `runExec` (from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/process-runtime`), not the Node.js built-in `execFile`. `runExec` delegates to execa with `forceKillAfterDelay: COMMAND_PROCESS_TREE_KILL_GRACE_MS` (300ms), providing a built-in two-phase kill: `SIGTERM` → 300ms grace → `SIGKILL`. Source: `src/process/exec.ts:50-63`, `src/process/exec-spawn.ts:7`.\n\n## Evidence Map\n\n| Layer | Detail |\n|-------|--------|\n| **Changed surface** | `execAz` in `extensions/microsoft-foundry/cli.ts:47-58` — one line |\n| **Node.js contract** | `execFileSync` default `killSignal` is `SIGTERM` (Node.js docs); no force-kill fallback on timeout |\n| **Callers** | `isAzCliInstalled:77`, `getLoggedInAccount:86`, `listSubscriptions:95`, `getAccessTokenResult:135` — all sync, all on gateway hot paths |\n| **Sibling** | `execAzAsync:60-73` uses `runExec` (`src/process/exec.ts:50-63`) with built-in `SIGTERM` → 300ms → `SIGKILL` — already safe |\n| **Mock test** | `index.test.ts:591` — verifies `execFileSyncMock` receives `killSignal: \"SIGKILL\"` |\n| **Behavioral proof (sync)** | `index.test.ts:604` — spawns real Node process ignoring `SIGTERM`, confirms `SIGKILL` terminates it within 2s |\n| **Behavioral proof (async)** | `index.test.ts:622` — spawns real Node process via `runExec`, confirms two-phase kill (SIGTERM → SIGKILL) terminates within 2s |\n| **Test suite** | 96/96 pass |\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Prevents hung `az` processes from blocking gateway sync operations\n- No behavioral change for successful `az` invocations\n- 30s timeout, encoding, and all other options unchanged",
